{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8231838",
      "title": "useEffect Not Needed: Another Example",
      "sourceHash": "2ce58b95c0e14f9f93215053339949a1fb9e0df0f7dc98b6bab765fa0ed67885",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 2.61,
          "en": "Now before we'll take another look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 3.51,
          "en": "at useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.51,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "let's stick at this local storage example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "because of course just storing items when we add them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "The local storage should also be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 17.64,
          "en": "when we remove a place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.64,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "by clicking on it here and confirming this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 24.81,
          "en": "And of course, I also wanna load my data from local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.81,
          "end": 28.02,
          "en": "when the app starts, so that when that happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.02,
          "end": 32.523,
          "en": "I pre-populate this box up here with my stored items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.84,
          "end": 36.69,
          "en": "Now let's start with the code for deleting items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.69,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 43.7,
          "en": "To do that, we again first need to fetch our stored IDs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "so that we can then update them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "And then we again need to update the stored items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 51.633,
          "en": "with a local storage 'setItem'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "and update them with help of this key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "And now the updated array in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "is based on the fetched existing array of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "And here we again need to create a stringified array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 69.243,
          "en": "and I'll create that array that should now be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.243,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "based on that stored IDs array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "with help of the filter method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "which is built into the browser, basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 80.01,
          "en": "and which allows us to produce a new array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.01,
          "end": 83.313,
          "en": "based on this array, and some filtering condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 88.08,
          "en": "For that filter takes a function that will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 90.81,
          "en": "on every item in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.81,
          "end": 95.25,
          "en": "and will get every item as an input to this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.25,
          "end": 97.32,
          "en": "And then we have to return true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "if we want to keep that item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 100.593,
          "en": "and false if we want drop it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 105.066,
          "en": "So therefore here, I'll simply check if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.066,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "the ID I am looking at here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 112.92,
          "en": "is not equal to 'selectedPlace.current',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.92,
          "end": 117.27000000000001,
          "en": "which is simply the ID of the place on which I clicked here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.27000000000001,
          "end": 120.48,
          "en": "when I'm clicking on it in my first box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.48,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "So if these two IDs do not match,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 126.57,
          "en": "I know that this is not the item I wanna delete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.57,
          "end": 130.11,
          "en": "therefore I'm returning true and I keep the item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 131.88,
          "en": "But if these IDs do match,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.88,
          "end": 133.98,
          "en": "this condition here will yield false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.98,
          "end": 137.61,
          "en": "and this ID will be removed from this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 139.95,
          "en": "And that's how we can store an updated array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.95,
          "end": 142.95,
          "en": "that does no longer contain this ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.95,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "Now last but not least, we of course also need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 149.01,
          "en": "to fetch these items when the app starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.01,
          "end": 151.11,
          "en": "And here you might again think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 153.723,
          "en": "that you probably need useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 157.5,
          "en": "because of course we could now use useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 162.5,
          "en": "just as we used it here with navigator geolocation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.84,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "And we could merge our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 168.45,
          "en": "into this existing useEffect usage, or use it again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.45,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "like all React hooks, you can use useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 173.913,
          "en": "as often as you want and need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 176.97,
          "en": "And you could therefore think that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.97,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "the code for retrieving our places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 182.567,
          "en": "should go into useEffect here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.567,
          "end": 185.845,
          "en": "So we can get our loaded places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.845,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "just as we're doing it down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 193.053,
          "en": "with help of local storage 'getItem', like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.7,
          "end": 197.1,
          "en": "And since these are only the IDs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.1,
          "end": 201.32999999999998,
          "en": "but I want to get places with all the place related data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.32999999999998,
          "end": 203.4,
          "en": "like the title and the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.4,
          "end": 208.32,
          "en": "we then need to map these IDs to actual place objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.32,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "By using the map method, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 216.6,
          "en": "to convert every ID to a complete place object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "And that can be done by taking this available places array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 223.35,
          "en": "which is coming from the data JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.35,
          "end": 226.65,
          "en": "which contains these place objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.65,
          "end": 230.7,
          "en": "And it's these objects to which I wanna map my IDs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "and we can perform that mapping",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "by using available places here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 241.863,
          "en": "and by then finding a place for the ID we're having here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "So 'find' then also takes another function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 250.14,
          "en": "And here we get every place from 'AVAILABLE_PLACES'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.14,
          "end": 252.57,
          "en": "passed in automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.57,
          "end": 254.468,
          "en": "And here I'm looking for the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.468,
          "end": 258.243,
          "en": "where the ID is equal to this ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.26,
          "end": 262.47,
          "en": "And this code here will then simply give us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.47,
          "end": 266.82,
          "en": "an array of place objects based on this array of IDs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.82,
          "end": 269.223,
          "en": "which we retrieve from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.45,
          "end": 275.45,
          "en": "And of course now we could call 'setPickedPlaces' here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 278.633,
          "en": "and set this equal to 'storedPlaces'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 280.17,
          "end": 282.9,
          "en": "Now when we add an empty dependencies array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.9,
          "end": 285.06,
          "en": "just as we did it down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.06,
          "end": 288.931,
          "en": "this effect function here will only run once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.931,
          "end": 291.78,
          "en": "after the app component function ran.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.78,
          "end": 295.11,
          "en": "And therefore will not enter an infinite loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 295.11,
          "end": 297.69,
          "en": "will fetch our data and populate our box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.69,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "with that fetched data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 301.05,
          "en": "We could do it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 304.53,
          "en": "And if I save that and I reload, you see indeed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.53,
          "end": 308.7,
          "en": "I'm starting with the places I previously added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 308.7,
          "end": 310.95,
          "en": "And if I delete a place and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 310.95,
          "end": 315.39,
          "en": "that place is gone but the other places are still fetched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 317.85,
          "en": "So this clearly works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.85,
          "end": 320.67,
          "en": "But this here is now an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.67,
          "end": 323.427,
          "en": "for a redundant usage of useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.444,
          "end": 328.65,
          "en": "Now, why is using useEffect like this redundant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.65,
          "end": 331.35,
          "en": "and actually not recommended?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.35,
          "end": 333.3,
          "en": "Because this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.3,
          "end": 335.79,
          "en": "where we use local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 340.79,
          "en": "unlike this code here where we gut the user's location,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 340.8,
          "end": 342.99,
          "en": "runs synchronously.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 342.99,
          "end": 346.35,
          "en": "Which means it basically finishes instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 346.35,
          "end": 348.21,
          "en": "It's executed line by line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 348.21,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "and once a line finished execution, it's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 354.21,
          "en": "We have the final result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 354.21,
          "end": 358.92,
          "en": "And this was not the case here for 'getCurrentPosition',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 358.92,
          "end": 362.7,
          "en": "when this line executed here it was not done yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.7,
          "end": 366.21,
          "en": "Instead it was only done once this callback function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 366.21,
          "end": 368.19,
          "en": "was executed by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.19,
          "end": 371.85,
          "en": "and that happened at some point in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 371.85,
          "end": 374.858,
          "en": "We can even see that it takes some time if we reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 374.858,
          "end": 378.873,
          "en": "because these places down here are not there instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 379.83,
          "end": 382.14,
          "en": "But for local storage, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 382.14,
          "end": 384.99,
          "en": "We got no callback function or promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 384.99,
          "end": 386.64,
          "en": "or anything like that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 386.64,
          "end": 390.48,
          "en": "Instead retrieving the data like this is instant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 390.48,
          "end": 393.15,
          "en": "And therefore this app component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.15,
          "end": 395.76,
          "en": "does not finish its execution cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 395.76,
          "end": 398.373,
          "en": "before fetching that data is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 399.36,
          "end": 402.24,
          "en": "We can therefore simply get rid of useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.24,
          "end": 404.94,
          "en": "and get rid of that state updating function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 404.94,
          "end": 406.35,
          "en": "which would be a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 406.35,
          "end": 409.38,
          "en": "because it would lead to an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 409.38,
          "end": 412.62,
          "en": "And we can simply move that code in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 412.62,
          "end": 417.62,
          "en": "of the state initialization code and use the stored places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 417.78,
          "end": 421.11,
          "en": "which again are available instantly here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 421.11,
          "end": 425.193,
          "en": "to initialize our picked places state like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 426.15,
          "end": 430.623,
          "en": "So to use the stored places as an initial state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 431.58,
          "end": 435.18,
          "en": "This works because this code runs synchronously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 435.18,
          "end": 437.67,
